    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1834, Randolph shipped 35,000–40,000 bales of cotton annually, outpacing Memphis at the time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ourtipton.com/posts/randolph-tennessee-the-rise-fall-and-legacy-of-a-forgotten-river-town/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s fortunes fell in the late 1840s when failed railroad plans and an unfavorable mail route cut it off from growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
